Swipe Keyboard

Keyboard source: https://github.com/itsdestin/swipe-keyboard. Copyright 2026 Destin Moss <https://youcoded.ai>.
The keyboard plugin and its tools are licensed GPL-2.0-only OR GPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-GPL, the
engine library (libswipekb_engine: swipe recognition and prediction) LGPL-2.1-only OR LGPL-3.0-only OR
LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-LGPL, following KDE's licensing policy; the licence texts are in LICENSES/ of the source and
in this licence folder. Every source file names its licence (SPDX header or REUSE.toml). Source revision and local
modifications are recorded in SOURCE-PROVENANCE.txt in the corresponding source archive. The source archive is a
required companion to binary build artifacts; these recipes do not publish anything.

The swipe engine (network runner, dictionary search, geometric decoder, sentence prior) is the project's own code.
No third-party engine code or model weights are included.

Word lists. The English swipe dictionary keeps every word, frequency and flag of the Android LatinIME/AOSP US English
word list (Apache-2.0, original notices retained; `Apache-2.0.txt` ships in `language-packs/`) and adds words counted
from FineWeb text. The Spanish, French and German swipe dictionaries and all `<language>.vocab.tsv` word lists are
counted from FineWeb / FineWeb-2 web text by Hugging Face (Open Data Commons Attribution License 1.0, `ODC-By-1.0.txt`;
derived from Common Crawl, whose terms of use also apply) plus Tatoeba sentences (CC BY 2.0 France). Only word counts
are kept, never text. No share-alike term applies; keep the attribution texts below. Transformation:
scripts/lm/count-words.py (counting) and scripts/dict/corpus_dictionary.py (filtering; rebuild with
scripts/dict/build-corpus-dictionaries.sh from the counts and the AOSP lists). Original AOSP input URLs/revisions/checksums
and the language files release are in assets.lock.json.
The English, Spanish, French and German next-word n-gram models, word lists and Spanish/French/German dictionaries (language files release `language-files-2026-10-22-open-words`, downloaded by checksum from assets.lock.json) are built from the same FineWeb / FineWeb-2 text plus Tatoeba sentences. They contain no third-party model weights. Retain each language's full Tatoeba contributor list (`<language>-CONTRIBUTORS.txt`), the Tatoeba notice (installed beside the package license at `share/licenses/swipe-keyboard/TATOEBA-CC-BY-2.0-FR.txt`, normally `/usr/share/licenses/...` or `/app/share/licenses/...`), `ODC-By-1.0.txt`, `Apache-2.0.txt` and `LANGUAGE-FILES-NOTICE.md` (all in `language-packs/`). Spanish Spain and Mexico share one Spanish model; hashes and provenance are in assets.lock.json and packaging/language-models/README.md. When English files are installed and verified, English next-word suggestions, completions and swipe ranking use the English n-gram; without them English swipes and completes from its dictionary, without next-word suggestions. These are small general baselines and make no region-specific Spanish or Gboard-parity claim.

Contextual prediction is language-specific; an unavailable or corrupt pack never falls back to English. Current-word completion uses the selected profile's own dictionary; next-word suggestions use that profile's model when available. On stock Plasma, next-word model input is limited to words this keyboard confirmed in the current field because raw application completion preferences are not fully exposed. Sensitive and restricted fields remain blocked. The bundled Deck backend retains its raw-policy bridge and stricter application vetoes.

Trained models. Models trained and released by Destin Moss via youcoded.ai, 2026 (SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Destin Moss <https://youcoded.ai>). The neural next-word models (`<language>.nwp.bin`, release `models-2026-10-23`) were trained on the same FineWeb / FineWeb-2 text (ODC-By 1.0, Hugging Face; Common Crawl) and Tatoeba sentences (CC BY 2.0 France) as the n-gram files and carry the same terms; keep the files and credits named above. The swipe model (`swipe-model.bin`, MIT; installed in `language-packs/`) was trained on real swipes from FUTO's swipe.futo.org dataset (MIT licence, Copyright (c) 2025 FUTO; text in `FUTO-SWIPE-DATA-LICENSE.txt` in the licence folder) plus synthetic swipes; it contains no third-party model weights. Details, sources and build scripts: `MODELS-NOTICE.md` in the licence folder.

Word lists for the guess bar: the swear-word lists (packaging/blocked-words) are from the LDNOOBW list, CC BY 4.0 (with
AOSP's offensive flags, Apache-2.0); the texting-word lists (packaging/texting-words) are the project's own, CC0 1.0.

Optional evaluation data is not included.
